data: {"delta":"Based on the most recent sources, here are the latest developments in space exploration:\n\nSpaceX's Starship successfully reached orbit for the first time but returned to Earth earlier than planned [2]. This represents a significant milestone in the development of the Starship spacecraft, though the early return suggests further refinements are needed.\n\nRegarding upcoming missions, Starship Flight 12 has a new launch date, and there's also progress on NASA's Artemis II moon mission [4]. The Artemis program aims to return humans to the moon, with Artemis II specifically planning to send astronauts on a lunar flyby.\n\nFor older context, in February 2023, a powerful solar storm delayed a SpaceX rocket launch and stalled oil rigs in Canada [5]. While not recent, this demonstrates how space weather can affect both space and ground-based operations.","conversationId":"cmvy07mv5000zk48kodwxnpav"}

